    <!-- Rambling speech with filler words and a self-correction (Friday, no wait, Saturday). Adapt it so it sounds natural when spoken in your language. -->
    <string name="profile_style_sample_dictation">um so I was thinking, like, we could grab dinner on Friday, no wait, Saturday, at that new Thai place, you know, the one by the park, the one that just opened, if you\'re free</string>
    <!-- The samples below show what each Rewriting (Keep, Fix, Polish) and Shorten (Off, Light, Strong) level makes of the sample dictation. Write them in full punctuation, with commas and a final full stop where natural; the app derives the Light and Minimal punctuation styles from them. -->
    <string name="profile_style_sample_keep_off">So I was thinking we could grab dinner on Saturday at that new Thai place, the one by the park, the one that just opened, if you\'re free.</string>
    <string name="profile_style_sample_keep_light">I was thinking we could grab dinner on Saturday at that new Thai place, the one by the park, if you\'re free.</string>
    <string name="profile_style_sample_keep_strong">Dinner on Saturday at that new Thai place, if you\'re free.</string>
    <string name="profile_style_sample_fix_off">I was thinking we could grab dinner on Saturday at the new Thai place by the park, the one that just opened, if you\'re free.</string>
    <string name="profile_style_sample_fix_light">I was thinking we could grab dinner on Saturday at the new Thai place by the park, if you\'re free.</string>
    <string name="profile_style_sample_fix_strong">Dinner on Saturday at the new Thai place by the park?</string>
    <string name="profile_style_sample_polish_off">Would you like to have dinner on Saturday? I was thinking of the new Thai restaurant by the park, which just opened.</string>
    <string name="profile_style_sample_polish_light">Would you like to have dinner on Saturday at the new Thai restaurant by the park?</string>
    <string name="profile_style_sample_polish_strong">Dinner on Saturday at the new Thai restaurant?</string>

